<article class="env-lemma" id="0D0S">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0D0S">Lemma <span data-tag="0D0S">75.8.3</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $X$ be a locally Noetherian algebraic space over $S$. If $L$ is in $D^+_{\textit{Coh}}(\mathcal{O}_ X)$ and $K$ in $D^-_{\textit{Coh}}(\mathcal{O}_ X)$, then $R\mathop{\mathcal{H}\! \mathit{om}}\nolimits (K, L)$ is in $D^+_{\textit{Coh}}(\mathcal{O}_ X)$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      We can check whether an object of $D(\mathcal{O}_ X)$ is in $D_{\textit{Coh}}(\mathcal{O}_ X)$ étale locally on $X$, see Cohomology of Spaces, Lemma <a href="/tag/07UB" data-tag="07UB">69.12.2</a>. Hence this lemma follows from the case of schemes, see Derived Categories of Schemes, Lemma <a href="/tag/0D0C" data-tag="0D0C">36.11.5</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>